messages:
maya: Quick sync — we need clearer guidance on 429/quota UX for SDK + console. Current messages are vague. Are we okay exposing per-key remaining vs only org-level?

alex: +1. Security concern if we expose per-key remaining in client-side SDKs. I'd prefer server responses include only a numeric "retry_after" and a code we can map to UI copy.

ram: For console UX, showing "Time until reset" + button to request quota increase is helpful. Also call out burst tokens: sometimes users see spikes that should be allowed if within burst budget.

devex-bot: Suggestion: standardize error payload: 
```
{
  "error": {
    "type": "rate_limit",
    "code": "org_quota_exceeded",
    "retry_after": 45,
    "scope": "org",
    "details_url": "https://docs.redwood.ai/rate-limits#org_quota"
  }
}
```

alex: That payload is good. Two asks: 1) add an optional "can_retry_immediately": false for throttles vs quota hits; 2) include a short "hint" string for the console to display.

ryan: For SDKs we can map code -> action: if code includes "burst_allowed" then surface "retry quickly" with exponential backoff. Otherwise show a polite block with contact link.

sre-bot: telemetry: emit metric `quota_event{scope,code}` and a boolean `burst_consumed`. Add trace id so we can correlate UI hits to infra traces.

maya: Agree. One policy question: do we ever disclose exact remaining tokens in hosted response? I worry about user-exposed secrets and DoS vectors.

ram: Let's avoid exposing exact remaining in public SDK responses. We can surface it in Console (authenticated) and Admin API (audited). SDKs get conservative signals only.

alex: Also update docs with 'best practice snippets' for retries. Short example for JS SDK:

```js
try {
  await client.generate(...)
} catch (e) {
  if (e.code === 'rate_limit' && e.retry_after) {
    await sleep(e.retry_after * 1000)
    // retry once
  }
}
```

maya: Action items: (1) eng-runtime to add `scope` + `details_url` to error payload (alex/ram) — due EOD Thu; (2) devex to draft SDK mapping + docs (ryan) — due Mon; (3) console to show admin-only remaining quota and add 'request increase' CTA (ram) — sync with design. Anyone object? :eyes: 

alex: no objections. :thumbsup: 

ryan: I'll start the doc PR.

devex-bot: Created ticket RW-4132 for SDK docs.

maya: thanks — let's keep replies short, will post RFC if anything changes.
